      DependencyIndex: 15
      LevelID: 69
      NodeType: 3
      Ports:
        Description:
          String: ""
        DescriptionText:
          ClassType1: TEXT
          String: |-
            Matcap reflections are a cheap way of doing reflection. The reflection is created by sampling from a spherical texture instead of actual scene data. This technique is also sometimes referred to as material capture ("MatCap") reflection. The reference texture only stores one side of a sphere.
            
            
            Inputs:
            Matcap Reflection Texture - the sphereical reflection map used to sample reflection lighting.
            Intensity - The strength of the reflection effect.
            Normal Space: the space that the normal has been calculated in. You can use World Space or Tangent Space (Normal Map) normals as input.
            Normal: the surface normal, provided in world or tangent space.
        FirstTime:
          Variable: false
        Locked:
          Variable: false
        SubGraphUniqueID7:
          ClassType2: TEXTURE_OBJECT_2D
          Connection0:
            NodeLevelID: 6
            PortID: Texture
        SubGraphUniqueID70:
          Connection0:
            NodeLevelID: 14
            PortID: Output
          Variable: [1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
        SubGraphUniqueID72:
          Variable: [1.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
        SubGraphUniqueID73:
          ItemIndex: 1
          ItemList: "World : Tangent (Normal Map)"
        SubGraphUniqueID74:
          Connection0:
            NodeLevelID: 16
            PortID: Output
          Variable: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
        SubGraphUniqueID78:
          IOType: 1
          Variable: [0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0]
        Title1:
          String: Matcap Reflection - Lock Rotation
      PositionX: -386
      PositionY: 116
